   "he": "עֵינוֹ אַחַת גְּדוֹלָה וְכוּ׳. תָּנָא: גְּדוֹלָה כְּשֶׁל עֵגֶל, קְטַנָּה כְּשֶׁל אַוָּוז.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches with regard to an animal where «one of its eyes» is «large» and one is small that this is a blemish. In this regard, it is «taught» in a baraita: When the mishna states the term «large,» it means the eye is as large «as» the eye «of a calf,» and when it states the term «small,» it means it is as small «as» that of «a goose.»"
